<h3 id=3D"consumer-rebalancing">Consumer rebalancing</h3>
<p>Consumer rebalancing decides which consumer is responsible for which sub=
set of partitions. The process could occur when a consumer joins, when a co=
nsumer leaves, when a consumer crashes, or when partitions are adjusted.</p=
>
<p>When consumer rebalancing occurs, the coordinator plays an important rol=
e. Let=E2=80=99s first take a look at what a coordinator is. The coordinato=
r is one of the brokers responsible for communicating with consumers to ach=
ieve consumer rebalancing. The coordinator receives heartbeat from consumer=
s and manages their offset on the partitions.</p>
<p>Let=E2=80=99s use an example to understand how the coordinator and the c=
onsumers work together.</p>
