group are connected to the same coordinator.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The coordinator maintains a joined consumer list. When the list changes,=
 the coordinator elects a new leader of the group.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>As the new leader of the consumer group, it generates a new partition di=
spatch plan and reports it back to the coordinator. The coordinator will br=
oadcast the plan to the other consumers in the group.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>In a distributed system, consumers might encounter all sorts of issues i=
ncluding network issues, crashes, restarts, etc. From the coordinator's per=
spective, they will no longer have heartbeats. When this happens, the coord=
inator will trigger a rebalance process to re-dispatch the partitions as il=
lustrated in Figure 17.</p>
