l</figcaption></div></figure>
<p><strong>ACK=3D1</strong></p>
<p>With ACK=3D1, the producer receives an ACK once the leader persists the =
message. The latency is improved by not waiting for data synchronization. I=
f the leader fails immediately after a message is acknowledged but before i=
t is replicated by follower nodes, then the message is lost. This setting i=
s suitable for low latency systems where occasional data loss is acceptable=
.</p>
